    "body": "Sweet, this works wonders!\r\nYes, my config is a little long .. thats why im in the process of factoring out one thing at a time. And since the new format syntax of starship allowed me to finally get rid of my quirky old prompt script, its already a lil faster. :)\r\n\r\nRevisiting the docs, its all there, but titled with \"Make sure your custom shell configuration exits gracefully\" and Powershell in there it didn't catch me.\r\n\r\n\"The custom command module runs the provided command in a shell instance, which is susceptible to being slowed down by your shell config.\" << this should be in the docs with a suitable headline and maybe one or two examples like zsh -d -f. I know about -f, but -d is also new for me. I bet it's not just me. 🙄\r\n\r\nThx very much!\r\n\r\n\r\nPS: in case you are interested, what all this config does .. here is a lil writeup: https://kakulukia.github.io/dotfiles/ and a short (:D) screencast ",
